{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G8VVNbdp57vCorVMJSa3sn","type":"tool_result","content":" M README.md\n M run.sh\n?? ANSWER.md\ndiff --git a/run.sh b/run.sh\nindex c41ad67..45b3f6f 100755\n--- a/run.sh\n+++ b/run.sh\n@@ -1,7 +1,8 @@\n #!/usr/bin/env bash\n # usage: run.sh <task> <lane> [rep]\n-# lanes: codex   Codex CLI, unsandboxed\n-#        kimi    Kimi Code under sandbox/agent.sb (no reading or writing the real home), scratch HOME\n+# lanes: codex            Codex CLI, unsandboxed\n+#        codex-sandboxed  Codex CLI under sandbox/agent.sb (no reading or writing the real home), scratch HOME\n+#        kimi             Kimi Code under sandbox/agent.sb (no reading or writing the real home), scratch HOME\n set -u\n D=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\" && pwd)\"\n T=$1; A=$2; REP=${3:-1}\n@@ -24,9 +25,26 @@ kimi_run() {\n   local rc=$?; rm -rf \"$SH\"; return $rc\n }\n \n+# Same Codex run under sandbox/agent.sb, with a scratch HOME and CODEX_HOME. Codex writes its last message to -o, and\n+# the profile denies writes to the real home, so -o points into the scratch folder in /tmp and the file is copied to\n+# the run folder after sandbox-exec returns (a denied -o write does not stop Codex: it only logs and exits 0).\n+# The profile also denies reads of the real home, so Codex's login and config are copied in before the sandbox starts.\n+codex_sandboxed_run() {\n+  local REAL=\"$HOME\" S; S=$(mktemp -d /tmp/hcodex-XXXXXX); mkdir -p \"$S/home\" \"$S/codex\"\n+  for f in auth.json config.toml; do [ -f \"$REAL/.codex/$f\" ] && cp \"$REAL/.codex/$f\" \"$S/codex/$f\"; done\n+  ( cd \"$W\" && export HOME=\"$S/home\" && sandbox-exec -D HOME=\"$REAL\" -f \"$D/sandbox/agent.sb\" \\\n+      env CODEX_HOME=\"$S/codex\" timeout $TO codex exec --skip-git-repo-check --dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox \\\n+      -C \"$W\" --json -o \"$S/final.txt\" \"$P\" < /dev/null > \"$R/agent.log\" 2> \"$R/agent.err\" )\n+  local rc=$?\n+  if [ -f \"$S/final.txt\" ]; then cp \"$S/final.txt\" \"$R/final.txt\"; else echo \"codex-sandboxed: no final.txt was written\" >&2; fi\n+  grep -q \"Operation not permitted\" \"$R/agent.err\" && echo \"codex-sandboxed: a write was denied by the sandbox, see agent.err\" >&2\n+  rm -rf \"$S\"; return $rc\n+}\n+\n start=$(date +%s)\n case $A in\n   codex) codex_run;;\n+  codex-sandboxed) codex_sandboxed_run;;\n   kimi)  kimi_run;;\n   *) echo \"unknown lane $A\"; exit 2;;\n esac","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7dc7bc5a-9614-455c-ae57-a04af4e8909b","uuid":"d5253fbc-6100-4ac6-9d9d-b552a71a1a79","timestamp":"2026-11-10T02:09:43.112Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":" M README.md\n M run.sh\n?? ANSWER.md\ndiff --git a/run.sh b/run.sh\nindex c41ad67..45b3f6f 100755\n--- a/run.sh\n+++ b/run.sh\n@@ -1,7 +1,8 @@\n #!/usr/bin/env bash\n # usage: run.sh <task> <lane> [rep]\n-# lanes: codex   Codex CLI, unsandboxed\n-#        kimi    Kimi Code under sandbox/agent.sb (no reading or writing the real home), scratch HOME\n+# lanes: codex            Codex CLI, unsandboxed\n+#        codex-sandboxed  Codex CLI under sandbox/agent.sb (no reading or writing the real home), scratch HOME\n+#        kimi             Kimi Code under sandbox/agent.sb (no reading or writing the real home), scratch HOME\n set -u\n D=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\" && pwd)\"\n T=$1; A=$2; REP=${3:-1}\n@@ -24,9 +25,26 @@ kimi_run() {\n   local rc=$?; rm -rf \"$SH\"; return $rc\n }\n \n+# Same Codex run under sandbox/agent.sb, with a scratch HOME and CODEX_HOME. Codex writes its last message to -o, and\n+# the profile denies writes to the real home, so -o points into the scratch folder in /tmp and the file is copied to\n+# the run folder after sandbox-exec returns (a denied -o write does not stop Codex: it only logs and exits 0).\n+# The profile also denies reads of the real home, so Codex's login and config are copied in before the sandbox starts.\n+codex_sandboxed_run() {\n+  local REAL=\"$HOME\" S; S=$(mktemp -d /tmp/hcodex-XXXXXX); mkdir -p \"$S/home\" \"$S/codex\"\n+  for f in auth.json config.toml; do [ -f \"$REAL/.codex/$f\" ] && cp \"$REAL/.codex/$f\" \"$S/codex/$f\"; done\n+  ( cd \"$W\" && export HOME=\"$S/home\" && sandbox-exec -D HOME=\"$REAL\" -f \"$D/sandbox/agent.sb\" \\\n+      env CODEX_HOME=\"$S/codex\" timeout $TO codex exec --skip-git-repo-check --dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox \\\n+      -C \"$W\" --json -o \"$S/final.txt\" \"$P\" < /dev/null > \"$R/agent.log\" 2> \"$R/agent.err\" )\n+  local rc=$?\n+  if [ -f \"$S/final.txt\" ]; then cp \"$S/final.txt\" \"$R/final.txt\"; else echo \"codex-sandboxed: no final.txt was written\" >&2; fi\n+  grep -q \"Operation not permitted\" \"$R/agent.err\" && echo \"codex-sandboxed: a write was denied by the sandbox, see agent.err\" >&2\n+  rm -rf \"$S\"; return $rc\n+}\n+\n start=$(date +%s)\n case $A in\n   codex) codex_run;;\n+  codex-sandboxed) codex_sandboxed_run;;\n   kimi)  kimi_run;;\n   *) echo \"unknown lane $A\"; exit 2;;\n esac","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01G8VVNbdp57vCorVMJSa3sn","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtS8VZreZMmraewDA16G","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added the `codex-sandboxed` lane to `run.sh`, documented it in `README.md`, and wrote `ANSWER.md`. I did not run the real Codex lane, because that sends the `fizz` task to OpenAI. Nothing is committed.\n\n**What the lane does**\n- It runs the same `codex exec` as the `codex` lane, wrapped in `sandbox/agent.sb` the way the kimi lane is wrapped.\n- It uses a scratch HOME and a scratch `CODEX_HOME` in `/tmp`.\n- `-o` writes to scratch, and `final.txt` is copied to the run folder after the sandbox exits. The sandbox denies writes to the real home, so a direct `-o` there would fail.\n- The lane warns if `agent.err` shows `Operation not permitted` or no `final.txt` was written.\n- I did not change `sandbox/agent.sb`.\n\n**Where the colleague's note applied**\n- The `-o` write into a denied folder applies, so I used the scratch-and-copy fix. I apply it on every run, not only when the run folder is under home.\n- The \"don't trust the exit code alone\" check applies, and the lane warns on it.\n- The Mistral Vibe `--output-dir` part does not apply, because there is no Mistral lane here.\n- The \"one smoke run with the grader\" step is not done, for the reason above.\n\n**One thing the README got wrong:** it says Codex needs nothing from the home folder because it uses `CODEX_API_KEY`. On this machine `CODEX_API_KEY` is unset and Codex logs in from `~/.codex/auth.json`. So the lane copies `auth.json` and `config.toml` into the scratch folder before the sandbox starts. That puts the login token where the sandboxed shell can read it, with network open. This is your call, and `ANSWER.md` lays out the two options.\n\n**Verification (no network calls)**\n- `bash -n` passes.\n- A full lane run with a stub `codex` on `PATH` worked: the login file reached scratch, `final.txt` was copied out, and no scratch folder was left behind.\n- A write to the real home from inside the lane was denied, and the warning fired.\n- The real `codex` 0.160.0 starts under the profile (`codex --version`).\n\n**Not verified:** a real Codex run, and the colleague's claim that Codex exits 0 after a denied `-o` write. Run `./run.sh fizz codex-sandboxed 1` once to confirm both. The test run folders and stub are removed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1319,"cache_read_input_tokens":46694,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1319},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7dc7bc5a-9614-455c-ae57-a04af4e8909b","uuid":"b69cc9f1-8966-4d3e-829c-91ee27363f54","timestamp":"2026-11-10T02:09:47.648Z","request_id":"req_011CgtS8VQBo7ZXbwjoePCjD"}
